{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"331","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B1. Shave Beaver!"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Smart Beaver has recently designed and built an innovative nanotechnologic all-purpose beaver mass shaving machine, \"Beavershave 5000\". Beavershave 5000 can shave beavers by families! How does it work? Very easily!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" beavers, each of them has a unique id from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consider a permutation "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" these beavers. Beavershave 5000 needs one session to shave beavers with ids from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" (inclusive) if and only if there are such indices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i1 < i2 < ... < ik"},{"kind":"text","text":", that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai1 = x"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai2 = x + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aik - 1 = y - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aik = y"},{"kind":"text","text":". And that is really convenient. For example, it needs one session to shave a permutation of beavers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1, 2, 3, ..., n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If we can't shave beavers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" in one session, then we can split these beavers into groups "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[x, p1]"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[p1 + 1, p2]"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[pm + 1, y]"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x ≤ p1 < p2 < ... < pm < y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", in such a way that the machine can shave beavers in each group in one session. But then Beavershave 5000 needs "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" working sessions to shave beavers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All beavers are restless and they keep trying to swap. So if we consider the problem more formally, we can consider queries of two types: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" what is the minimum number of sessions that Beavershave 5000 needs to shave beavers with ids from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive? "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" two beavers on positions "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the beavers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ax"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ay"},{"kind":"text","text":") swapped. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can assume that any beaver can be shaved any number of times."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the total number of beavers, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":". The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated integers — the initial beaver permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of queries, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ q ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":". The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the queries. Each query "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" looks as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yi"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the query type ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is to shave beavers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yi"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" is to swap beavers on positions "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yi"},{"kind":"text","text":"). All queries meet the condition: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ xi < yi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" to get 30 points, you need to solve the problem with constraints: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":" (subproblem B1); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" to get 100 points, you need to solve the problem with constraints: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n ≤ 3·105"},{"kind":"text","text":" (subproblems B1+B2). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the number of queries "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" is limited "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ q ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":" in both subproblem B1 and subproblem B2."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", print the minimum number of Beavershave 5000 sessions."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n1 3 4 2 5\n6\n1 1 5\n1 3 4\n2 2 3\n1 1 5\n2 1 5\n1 1 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n1\n3\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B1","problemCode":"331B1","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/331/problem/B1"}